---
# LLVM defaults, overridden only where the house style differs: 4-space indent,
# 100-column lines, `Type* ptr`, un-indented namespaces, indented case labels.
# Everything else — include sorting, trailing-comment alignment, and the
# one-liner rules — is left at LLVM's defaults on purpose.
#
# The whole tree is formatted with this config and every file is at its
# formatting fixed point, so a `--dry-run` check over the tree passes clean.
# `clang-format -i` on files you touch keeps it that way. Vendored code is
# excluded via .clang-format-ignore.
#
# One gotcha if you ever re-sweep: clang-format is not always idempotent in a
# single pass (wrapped trailing comments in an aligned block can settle on the
# second pass), and `-i` runs exactly one. Re-run until the tree stops
# changing rather than assuming one pass is enough.
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM

IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 100
AccessModifierOffset: -4
NamespaceIndentation: None
IndentCaseLabels: true

PointerAlignment: Left
ReferenceAlignment: Left
